-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. Machine-checked algebraic invariants
-- Proved directly in Word arithmetic (zero postulates!) over linproof.cub's plusw / mulw:
-- Exact doubly-ruled hyperboloid surface invariant (Brahmagupta-Fibonacci form at c = 1, d = u):
--   For any circle point (a, b) and ruling parameter u,
--   (a + u·b)² + b² + (u·a)² ≡ (a² + b²) · (1 + u²) + 2·a·(u·b),
--   proving every straight 3D ruling line (y, z) = (a + u·b, b − u·a) lies identically on the
--   one-sheeted hyperboloid y² + z² = (a² + b²)(1 + u²).
wsq : Word → Word
wsq x = mulw x x
